<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ardo Njobdi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">19th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ardo Njobdi was a Fulbe leader who founded Ngaoundere around 1835 under the authority of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adamawa-emirate">Adamawa Emirate</a>. His forces conquered the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mbum-people">Mbum people</a> of the Adamawa plateau in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cameroon">Cameroon</a>. The lamidate he founded became one of the main slave-raiding states of the region, and his successors still reign there as lamidos.</p></div>
